@24:12 "Learning how to code means thinking in a specific way"

As a developer with almost 40 years experience: They do not think in that way yet. But they are at "good intern" stage, and any day now they're going to receive that "head twist", and then they'll go Junior -> Senior -> Principal -> Genius in an afternoon.

Well, ..., : "Genuis" might take a few more hours

@23:00 think it is possible to come to the opposite conclusion - that coding will be amongst the last things "to fall", precisely because code is verifiable.

Writing a poem, a story, a book, a screenplay.. that's easy, there is practically no objectively wrong answer.

Writing code, that works, properly, for all edge cases, for something of decent scope and scale.. that's a whole different ballpark of difficult
